"""a20 — declarative instance runner for A20OS.

Reads an instance manifest (TOML under instances/), validates it, derives
the corresponding Makefile variables, and delegates execution to make. The
Makefile remains the build engine; this tool owns configuration derivation.
See docs/instances.md for the manifest reference.

# ─── How to run ───
#   tools/a20 check                        validate every instances/*.toml
#   tools/a20 check-registry               validate components/drivers.toml
#   tools/a20 list                         list known instances
#   tools/a20 show-vars qemu-riscv64       print derived make variables
#   tools/a20 build   qemu-riscv64         make <vars> dev-build|kernel-only
#   tools/a20 run     qemu-riscv64-gui     build + boot in QEMU
#   tools/a20 debug   qemu-riscv64         build -O0 -g + qemu -S -s (GDB)
#   tools/a20 test    smoke-riscv64        build, boot, inject commands, grep log
#   tools/a20 flash   stm32f103-xuanwu     build firmware + OpenOCD flash
#   tools/a20 package vbox-iso-x86_64      build + assemble a release artifact
# Extra arguments after `--` are passed to make verbatim, e.g.
#   tools/a20 build qemu-riscv64 -- -j8
"""

